{
  "id": "Compound::DB01424 - Gene::1544",
  "verbalization": "Aminophenazone is shown to interact with Cyp1a2 through a series of mechanistic pathways that involve the cytochrome P450 family. The drug binds to Cyp2c9 and Cyp3a4, both of which are involved in oxidative metabolism, and these enzymes are themselves part of the oxidoreductase activity that is also associated with Cyp1a2. This suggests a potential pathway where Aminophenazone may influence Cyp1a2 through the activation or inhibition of its substrates. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Aminophenazone's interaction with Cyp1a2 is mediated through the shared role of Cyp2c9 and Cyp3a4 in catalyzing metabolic reactions, which in turn may modulate Cyp1a2's activity. The final scores suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct involvement of Cyp1a2 in the drug's metabolic effects.",
